  "masks": "V is finite reference RGB. E is V and finite prediction RGB. Y is mean FP32 absolute RGB channel error > FP32(0.05) on E. S is E and all five scores finite.",
  "state": "Operating states on E: high finite score >= fixed threshold, low strictly below, unknown nonfinite. Keep V as coverage denominator. Recompute constant and 1-alpha directly; cross-check L0 independent archived baseline and learned states.",
  "AP": "Independent sklearn.metrics.average_precision_score(binary labels, unaltered finite score), grouped ties. Single class or empty S is undefined. View AP -> within-family eligible view mean -> four-family eligible mean. Coverage L/V, accepted risk LY/L pool counts within family then give eligible families equal weight. Missed errors LY+UY.",
  "tolerance": "Counts and S/V/E mask hashes exact. Unitless metrics absolute 1e-12. No tuning. Old comparison and public summaries are read only after raw computation to test agreement."
